%description:

Tcp.tcpAlgorithmClass:westwood -- Westwood sets a threshold at a fast retransmit and inflates the window with each further duplicate ACK.

The claim (Tcp.ned): "the NED type of the algorithm of each connection"; TcpWestwood sets the
threshold from its estimate of the bandwidth.

The classes: the nine algorithms of the package inet.transportlayer.tcp.flavours (TcpNewReno is
the default, TcpReno the value of LegacyTcp, TcpCubic of LinuxTcp), qualified-alias (a
qualified NED type name), unknown (a name without a NED type: an error) and socket-override
(the open command of a socket selects another algorithm). Each test of an algorithm checks a
behavior that none of the other eight algorithms shows. The code:
TcpConnection::createTcpAlgorithm() and the classes of the algorithms. This test separates TcpWestwood: TcpVegas inflates the window too but sets no threshold at
a fast retransmit, TcpNewReno, TcpReno, DcTcp and TcpCubic keep the window flat during the
recovery, TcpTahoe drops it to one segment, and TcpNoCongestionControl and DumbTcp have no
window.

Host under test: host1, without SACK, which sends 100000 bytes; the round trip is 40 ms, and
the tap drops the 15th data segment once. Observation: level 2, a slow-start threshold at the
loss, then a window of at least two segments, and then a larger window: the next duplicate
ACK adds a segment. The threshold comes in the same instant as the fast retransmission, which
separates it from the threshold that TcpVegas sets when it leaves slow start.

%# parameter: Tcp.tcpAlgorithmClass
%# class: westwood
%# value: "TcpWestwood"
%# key: *.host1.tcp.tcpAlgorithmClass
%# expected-result: PASS

%includes:
#include "ProtocolTest.h"

%global:

using namespace inet;
using namespace inet::protocoltest;

Define_ProtocolTestProgram()
{
    return ProtocolTest("TcpAlgorithmClassWestwood")
        .intercept(tap("tap").from("host1").filterPacket("tcp.sequenceNo == {isn} + 1 + 14 * 1448 && ipv4.totalLengthField > 100B").nth(1).drop()
                     .describe("the 15th data segment of host1, the first time"))
        .once(on("host1.tcp").signal("packetSentToLower")
             .filterPacket("tcp.synBit == true && tcp.ackBit == false")
             .capture("isn", "tcp.sequenceNo")
             .describe("the SYN of host1")
             .within(0.5))
        .once(on("host1.tcp").signal("ssthresh")
                  .filterValueAtMost(1e8)
                  .describe("the slow-start threshold at the fast retransmit")
                  .within(1.5))
        .once(on("host1.tcp").signal("packetSentToLower")
                  .filterPacket("tcp.sequenceNo == {isn} + 1 + 14 * 1448 && pk.dataLength > tcp.headerLength")
                  .describe("the fast retransmission, in the same instant as the threshold")
                  .within(1e-9))
        .once(on("host1.tcp").signal("cwnd")
                  .first()
                  .captureMax("windowAtLoss", "value")
                  .assertValueAtLeast(2896)
                  .describe("the window at the fast retransmit, at least two segments")
                  .within(0.001))
        .once(on("host1.tcp").signal("cwnd")
                  .first()
                  .assertEvent([](const MatchContext& context) { return context.event.value > context.get("windowAtLoss").doubleValue(); })
                  .describe("the next window, larger: the inflation by a duplicate ACK")
                  .within(0.1));
}

%activity:
EV << "TcpAlgorithmClassWestwood compiled\n";

%inifile: omnetpp.ini

[General]
*.host1.tcp.tcpAlgorithmClass = "TcpWestwood"    # the parameter under test
*.linkDelay = 10ms
*.host1.app[0].sendBytes = 100000B
*.host1.tcp.sackSupport = false
include ../../parameter/ini/_bulk.ini
include ../../parameter/ini/_base.ini

%contains: stdout
PROTOCOLTEST TcpAlgorithmClassWestwood: PASS
